assertionResults.fullName:
blocked on out-of-write-set wiring — see .agent-notes/cdd-B7FU-R2.md for the exact mechanism a self-embedding CLASS body ("class C { {{ class C { ... } }} }") throws EmbeddedDiagramDepthError through a real renderSync(...) call -- NOT reachable at ANY depth >= 2 today, for a reason MORE PRECISE than the isEnhancedBody gap above: src/diagrams/class/parser.ts#handlePendingBodyLine tests EVERY body line against the bare "}" close-body regex unconditionally (no embedded-block awareness at parse time, unlike the TYPE0/TYPE1 path class-embedded-block.ts/class-multiline-element.ts already solve for "[ ... ]" bodies) -- a nested class declaration's OWN closing "}" inside a {{ }} region prematurely closes the OUTER class body before the embed is ever collected, regardless of isEnhancedBody or the recursion guard. Verified by direct probe (2026-09-22): "class C {
--
{{
class C {
--
{{
field
}}
}
}}
}" renders a "Syntax Error?" refusal box, not a depth error. The guard itself IS proven, at the renderer-unit level, in class-nested-diagram-renderer.test.ts (4 tests, real depth accounting, no mock).

